Z||000012||Formula88||08-07-2001||09:17 AM||||I always did LOVE the Countach!  I don't know if it's true or not, but countach is an expletive in Italian (don't know which one) and it's rumoured that was the remark by a bystander as the first Countach rolled off the truck at the car show for it's unveiling.  Thus, the car's name was born.  Like I said, I don't know if that's true, but it's a cool story.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000013||JSocha||08-07-2001||09:28 AM||||Loosely translated in Italian, Countach, I believe meant or means "Oh my God".  Apparently some guy visiting the Lamborghini factory said that when the first one rolled off the assembly line and it stuck.  Been awhile since I seen the documentary of Lamborghini.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
